-- title:
--   Transitions are surjective on Hopf kernels of a quotient map
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a local commutative ring and $p$ a prime. Let $G$ and $T$ be $p$-divisible groups over $R$ of heights $h$ and $t$ in the sense of the project's structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): families $v \mapsto G.\mathrm{level}\,v$, $T.\mathrm{level}\,v$ of commutative, cocommutative $R$-Hopf algebras that are finite and free as $R$-modules, equipped with surjective $R$-bialgebra transition maps $\mathrm{level}(v+1) \to \mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^{v}$, and with $\operatorname{rank}_R \mathrm{level}\,v = p^{vh}$ (respectively $p^{vt}$). Let $\pi_v : G.\mathrm{level}\,v \to T.\mathrm{level}\,v$ be $R$-bialgebra maps, each surjective, compatible with the transitions in the sense that $\pi_{v+1}$ followed by $T.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ equals $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ followed by $\pi_v$ for all $v$. Then for each $v$ the map $G.\mathrm{transition}\,v$ sends the set underlying $\mathrm{hopfKer}(\pi_{v+1})$ onto the set underlying $\mathrm{hopfKer}(\pi_v)$; here, for a bialgebra map $\pi : A \to B$, $\mathrm{hopfKer}(\pi)$ is the $R$-subalgebra of $A$ on which the composite of the comultiplication with $\mathrm{id}_A \otimes \pi$ agrees with $a \mapsto a \otimes 1$, i.e. the right coinvariants. The assertion is the inclusion $\mathrm{hopfKer}(\pi_v) \subseteq G.\mathrm{transition}\,v\,[\,\mathrm{hopfKer}(\pi_{v+1})\,]$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity step in the construction of the quotient of a $p$-divisible group by a closed $p$-divisible subgroup: the coinvariant subalgebras $\mathrm{hopfKer}(\pi_v)$ are the coordinate rings of the quotients $G_v/T_v$, and the statement provides the surjective transition maps of that quotient system. It is used by the variant [`PDivisibleGroup.surjOn_transition_hopfKer_of_surjective_of_comp_eq_of_isPrincipalIdealRing`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.surjOn_transition_hopfKer_of_surjective_of_comp_eq_of_isPrincipalIdealRing).
